    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36341" root="قوب" body-key="q">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قُوَبٌ</span></b>  [in the two phrases here following is
probably pl. of ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قُوبَةٌ</span></b> ]. You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِى الأَرْضِ قُوَبٌ</span>
<i>In the ground are hollows</i> [app. meaning <i>round
hollows:</i> see 1, first sentence]. (A.) And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِى</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَأْسِهِ وَجِلْدِهِ قُوَبٌ</span> <i>In his head and his skin are
pits.</i> (A, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And hence ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">القُوَبَآءُ</span></b> . (A.)
See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قُوَبَآءُ</span>, in two places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  It signifies [also]
<i>Egg-shells.</i> (O, K.)

